The «BIMopen» interface style bundles:
- Inter 4.1 by The Inter Project Authors (https://github.com/rsms/inter), subset, licensed
  under the SIL Open Font License 1.1: crates/ui-egui/assets/fonts/inter/ (LICENSE.txt);
- icons of Lucide (lucide-static 1.55.0, https://lucide.dev), licensed under the ISC License:
  the SVG sources in crates/ui-egui/assets/icons/lucide/ (LICENSE), converted to
  crates/ui-egui/src/style_bimopen/lucide.rs.

Drawings and exported images write Arabic text with Noto Sans Arabic (Copyright 2010,
2012-2020 Google Inc.; 2015-2020 Google LLC; The Noto Project Authors), licensed under the
SIL Open Font License 1.1: crates/render/assets/fonts/ (OFL.txt).

The textures of the materials (crates/render/assets/textures/) come from ambientCG
(https://ambientcg.com) and are in the public domain under the Creative Commons CC0 1.0
Universal dedication; every texture's source is listed in LICENSES.md in that folder.

The «Realistico» visual style evaluates the analytic sky model of Lukas Hosek and Alexander
Wilkie with the coefficients of their reference implementation (CIE XYZ datasets),
Copyright (c) 2012 - 2013, Lukas Hosek and Alexander Wilkie, published under the 3-clause
BSD license (reproduced in crates/ui-egui/src/realistic/hosek_data.rs).

The moon of the «Realistico» sky (crates/ui-egui/assets/moon/moon-256x128.r8) is the colour map
of the CGI Moon Kit of NASA's Scientific Visualization Studio (https://svs.gsfc.nasa.gov/4720,
lroc_color_poles_1k.jpg, 2019; visualizer Ernie Wright, USRA; from the Lunar Reconnaissance
Orbiter camera team's WAC mosaic), reduced to grey at 256 × 128. NASA's Scientific
Visualization Studio publishes its content in the public domain unless otherwise noted
(https://svs.gsfc.nasa.gov/help/) and asks for this credit: NASA's Scientific Visualization
Studio. No NASA insignia or endorsement is implied.

The stars of the «Realistico» sky (crates/model/src/stars.rs) are the 1,604 stars brighter
than magnitude 5 of the Yale Bright Star Catalogue, 5th revised edition (D. Hoffleit and
W. H. Warren Jr., Astronomical Data Center, NASA/NSSDC, 1991; CDS/VizieR catalogue V/50,
DOI 10.26093/cds/vizier), keeping only position (J2000), visual magnitude and B−V colour.
The catalogue's ReadMe carries no copyright notice; VizieR asks that the authors and the
catalogue be cited, as here.
